{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1122519-sidhe-and-houses","id":1122519,"title":"Sidhe and Houses","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-29T15:28:15-07:00","id":1122519,"title":"Sidhe and Houses","content":"So, I have a few questions:<br /> <br /> Do all Sidhe have to belong to a House or could some of them be unaffiliated? Could a Sidhe be disowned by their House for example?<br /> <br /> Can new House be created? If yes, could commoner kiths create one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T19:00:27-07:00","id":1122566,"title":"","content":"The way sidhe are described in the books they all have a House affiliation. However, if I remember correctly there are a few examples of sidhe turning their back on their House. I would say this is quite rare, though the possibility of &quot;ronin&quot; sidhe could make for some interesting stories. But if you go by canon the sidhe are as much defined by their House as they are by their kith. In the Books of Houses there are multiple examples of oaths of allegiance to the different Houses. I've taken this as being what each sidhe does upon being sained and what commoners do when being accepted into a House.<br /> <br /> Canonically there are no methods for creating a new House. But there are plenty of them that have been created and circulated online by fans over the years. All of the Houses start with a founder after whom they are named. In all cases that founder was a powerful True Fae from before the Shattering. That founder's power helped create the House as their followers pledged allegiance to them, and the Dreaming has kept that power and those abilities over time. In order to make a new House you would need a similar founder and similar oaths of allegiance. Since the Shattering there wouldn't be anyone with enough power or pure enough fae to set things up as with the canonical Houses. <br /> <br /> As far as commoners creating a House. Why would they? Remember that commoners vs. nobles is something entrenched in the Dreaming itself and not just a societal structure. You would need a single commoner with the purity and power of a true fae sidhe, who was recognized by the Dreaming as true nobility equaling Dougal, Ailil, Gwydion, Scathach, or any of the other founders. I simply don't see that happening. I also don't think that you would find most commoners open to the idea of becoming nobility of this level when most of them fought against the sidhe during the Resurgence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T09:45:59-07:00","id":1123048,"title":"","content":"Speaking of which, I was wondering what would happen if a sidhe changeling had his Chrysalis, remember being from, say, House Eiluned, and there would be no other member of House Eiluned in the town/ city. Would it be the duty of the local lord to send words to House Eiluned had one of their own to look after, especially come the day of her Fior-Righ?<br /> <br /> Or, imagine the same situation, and there is no sidhe at all, only commoners who adopted the fledgling sidhe in their motley, never sending word to the nobility in another town.<br /> <br /> Even if a Saining could be performed, would the fledgling sidhe go into Bedlam without her full recognition by her fellow nobles?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T15:12:19-07:00","id":1123192,"title":"","content":"I admit to frequently wondering if Changeling should've just made <i>everyone</i> be a member of one noble house or another, regardless of what Kith they were. (Given how much focus the original game line gave to the nobility compared to commoners in terms of what was in the books, it might've made more sense.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T15:42:00-07:00","id":1123206,"title":"","content":"Most Changeling I've played has been very anti-nobility commoner games, and any sidhe PCs are no higher than title 2 and get snubbed by the other sidhe because they're slumming it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T00:39:24-07:00","id":1123348,"title":"","content":"Don't like the idea sidhe born into a house at all. I prefer to make it an individual decision to join a house.<br /> Not joining a house would be against the Dreaming and therefore a banality breaking point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/571-nin","name":"Nin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T16:10:35-07:00","id":1123680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1122519-sidhe-and-houses?p=1123192#post1123192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit to frequently wondering if Changeling should've just made <i>everyone</i> be a member of one noble house or another, regardless of what Kith they were. (Given how much focus the original game line gave to the nobility compared to commoners in terms of what was in the books, it might've made more sense.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why would that make more sense? If everyone was nobility then that completely negates any idea of commoner vs. noble. It keeps nobility from being anything special, and negates a large part of the idea behind the existence of the sidhe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T16:13:49-07:00","id":1123684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mattboggan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1122519-sidhe-and-houses?p=1123048#post1123048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of which, I was wondering what would happen if a sidhe changeling had his Chrysalis, remember being from, say, House Eiluned, and there would be no other member of House Eiluned in the town/ city. Would it be the duty of the local lord to send words to House Eiluned had one of their own to look after, especially come the day of her Fior-Righ?<br /> <br /> Or, imagine the same situation, and there is no sidhe at all, only commoners who adopted the fledgling sidhe in their motley, never sending word to the nobility in another town.<br /> <br /> Even if a Saining could be performed, would the fledgling sidhe go into Bedlam without her full recognition by her fellow nobles?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that it would be the responsibility of the local lord/lady to send word to someone of the new sidhe's house. I see it as sort of an unwritten rule between nobles to keep fostering the existence of noble houses. Having an area with NO sidhe at all would be pretty uncommon, and in modern society all you would have to do was go to the closest large town to find kithmates. I think that if you were the ONLY representative of a given kith in an area you'd want find others like you. This is true of any kith, not just sidhe.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T17:40:55-07:00","id":1123719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1122519-sidhe-and-houses?p=1123680#post1123680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Why would that make more sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, the game, especially in it's first and much of it's second editions, seemed entirely preoccupied with the doings of the Nobility - the Nobles sourcebook was, IIRC, one of the earliest books released; with the Commoner book literally being the last (before Arthaus tried to save the line) - with commoners seeming to get a minimum of coverage outside of the Kithbooks. If the developer and authors were so entranced by the nobility, they may has well have made them the entire focus of the game, with some sort of &quot;Guide to the Commoner Revolution&quot; coming later (the way Vampire originally did with the Sabbat). The entire commoner vs noble angle might've been more interesting had, prior to the Arthaus released War in Concordia, any event about it not been part of the past in a setting with an incredibly static political system. As for the Sidhe, their status as the epitome of nobility never struck me as being dependent on each of them getting an extra beanie, nor would it be in anyway diminished by a game heavily steeped in the sociopolitical intrigue and other doings of a half dozen or more competing Houses. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T08:58:08-07:00","id":1125248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1122519-sidhe-and-houses#post1122519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I have a few questions:<br /> <br /> Do all Sidhe have to belong to a House or could some of them be unaffiliated? Could a Sidhe be disowned by their House for example?</div> </div> </div> </div>It says on pg 117 of the 2nd edition main book that not all Sidhe join a house.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12192-rabdos","name":"Rabdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12192_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T09:57:38-07:00","id":1127181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1122519-sidhe-and-houses?p=1125248#post1125248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It says on pg 117 of the 2nd edition main book that not all Sidhe join a house.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, thank you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T19:35:09-07:00","id":1127448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1122519-sidhe-and-houses?p=1125248#post1125248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It says on pg 117 of the 2nd edition main book that not all Sidhe join a house.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good catch. However, there never seems to be any other mention of that or examples in any of the books or novels. It makes a certain sense that there would be some unaffiliated sidhe, but personally I see them as the rare exception, and they would likely be shunned or at least looked down upon by the other sidhe with House alignments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T01:33:43-08:00","id":1174803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1122519-sidhe-and-houses#post1122519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I have a few questions:<br /> <br /> Do all Sidhe have to belong to a House or could some of them be unaffiliated? Could a Sidhe be disowned by their House for example?<br /> <br /> Can new House be created? If yes, could commoner kiths create one?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The sidhe are the true blooded nobility of the Fae, so they automatically belong to one of the noble houses by default. A sidhe with no house is like a king with no lineage, it doesn't make any sense.<br /> <br /> The other kiths, however, were born as commoners and they had to work their asses off to achieve the same level of prestige that the sidhe are born into. So for them, joining a noble house is optional.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for founding a new noble house, sure it's possible. If a noble decided they wanted to start a family descended from their own legacy instead of one of their ancestors. But as for the commoners starting up a house, I would say the answer is a resounding <b><i>&quot;NO!&quot;</i></b><br /> <br /> It's not just the sidhe who harbored prejudice against the common folk, even the Dreaming itself chose to abandon them once the sidhe made their grand return. The commoners had spent hundreds of years keeping the Dreaming alive and cared for, but the moment the sidhe came back and told them to hand everything over, the Dreaming happily complied with their demands, much to the outrage of the commoners.<br /> <br /> <br /> Your question makes the mistake of assuming that the fae live and think as we do, when in actuality, thinking as we do is exactly what's killing them. The fae are not humans, they are the living embodiment of our dreams and aspirations. Those of the Arcadian sidhe were born from the dreams and aspirations of medieval nobility. <i>Which basically means that as far as they are concerned, the sidhe are objectively superior to the commoners.</i> The commoners are not their equals, and even considering the possibility would have made you a laughing stock of the community. In fact, that's exactly what happened to the Autumn sidhe when they showed up and offered to help their Arcadian cousins adjust to the modern world. The Arcadians took one look at them and declared they had become tainted beyond recognition.<br /> <br /> That's why they didn't ask the commoners to hand over their freeholds, they demanded that they do so. And when they tried to fight back, the nobility took it by force until the high king negotiated peace between them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Those of the Autumn sidhe, however, chose to stay in our world, instead of fleeing to Arcadia, and were slowly changed by exposure to mortal society over the centuries. They've worked alongside the commoners, hand in hand to rebuild and sustain the community across the generations. So they would be more willing to view them in a positive light.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> From the way I see it, the main difference between Arcadian and Autumn nobles is that the former had their power handed to them on a silver platter, while the later put in the time and effort to prove themselves worthy of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-10-2018, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T12:32:54-07:00","id":1452366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1122519-sidhe-and-houses?p=1123348#post1123348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't like the idea sidhe born into a house at all. I prefer to make it an individual decision to join a house.<br /> Not joining a house would be against the Dreaming and therefore a banality breaking point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the person suggesting that might not realize that ALL members of a house are considered nobility technically, even if they hold no actual title. It is entirely possible to be a Sidhe with no title, but you're still nobility because you're part of a house.<br /> <br /> Of course, the C20 PG is out now which has Banner Houses, so that expands options quite a bit in some ways. And I also have never seen a Sidhe mentioned in any of the material who did not join a house. For one, you'd either have to be a brand new soul or somebody with no recollection of your past who didn't get sained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","user":"Windthin","date":". 06-15-2021, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}